    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">What Is Artificial Intelligence?</title>
      <p>Artificial Intelligence (AI) refers to the simulation of human intelligence in machines that are programmed to think, learn, and problem-solve. AI encompasses a variety of subfields, including machine learning, deep learning, natural language processing, and computer vision.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Overview of AI Technologies</title>
      <p><b>Machine Learning (ML):</b> A subset of AI where algorithms enable machines to learn from data without explicit programming. It's widely used for tasks like prediction, classification, and pattern recognition.</p>
      <p><b>Deep Learning:</b> A more advanced subset of machine learning involving neural networks with many layers. Deep learning is crucial for complex tasks like image recognition and autonomous driving.</p>
      <p><b>Natural Language Processing (NLP):</b> This enables machines to understand, interpret, and generate human language, enabling voice assistants, chatbots, and language translation systems.</p>
      <p><b>Computer Vision:</b> A field within AI that enables computers to interpret and understand visual data, used in applications such as facial recognition and autonomous vehicles.</p>
    </section>
